   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the county law and the tax law, in relation to authorizing the\ncounty of Broome to impose an additional surcharge to pay for the costs\nassociated with updating the telecommunication equipment and telephone\nservices needed to provide an enhanced 911 emergency telephone system to serve\nsuch county; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration\nthereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S4392",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4392-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §336, County L; amd §186-g, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "County Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4392\n\nSPONSOR: AKSHAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the county law and the tax law, in\nrelation to authorizing the county of Broome to impose an additional\nsurcharge to pay for the costs associated with updating the telecommuni-\ncation equipment and telephone services needed to provide an enhanced\n911 emergency telephone system to serve such county; and providing for\nthe repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to impose an additional surcharge on wireless\ncommunications and landline services to fund the county's Public Safety\nRadio Capital project. This legislation is at the request of Broome\nCounty.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Section 303 of the county law is amended by adding a new\nsubdivision 4. Section 2: Establishes the effect date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nBroome County has requested home rule legislation to impose a surcharge\non wireless communications and landline services to fund the County's\nPublic Safety Radio Capital project. Currently, Broome County's emergen-\ncy communication systems consists of 12 different radio systems and are\noutdated and many of the systems have not been updated since the 1970's.\nThe use of outdated equipment has lead to gaps in coverage, which has\nresulted in first responders not being able to communicate during times\nof emergency.\n\nThe County's Public Safety Radio Capital project will address issues of\noutdated technology with new radios and radio towers that will allow\nemergency personnel to better communicate with dispatch and one another.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThis legislation will have no fiscal implications for State. The funds\nraised by the surcharge will be used by the County for upgrades to its\nemergency communications systems.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and be deemed repealed ten years\nafter it shall have become a law.\n",
